Both `mantest` and `shtest` failures are pre-existing on the baseline (same `FAIL: 2` before my change), so they're unrelated environment/valgrind issues.

## Summary

Fixed the assertion failure by validating JSON text at argument-parse time in `src/main.c` (matching the upstream fix for jqlang/jq#2572). Instead of appending the invalid `jv` returned by `jv_parse()` into `$ARGS` (which later aborted in `jv_dump_term`), both code paths — the `--` args-done path (src/main.c:237) and the post-program path (src/main.c:250) — now check `jv_is_valid()` and bail out early:

```c
jv v = jv_parse(argv[i]);
if (!jv_is_valid(v)) {
  fprintf(stderr, "%s: Invalid JSON text passed to --jsonargs\n", progname);
  die();
}
ARGS = jv_array_append(ARGS, v);
```

Verified:
- `./jq -n --jsonargs '$ARGS' 123 'invalid json'` now errors cleanly with exit code 2 (no assert/abort)
- The `--` path (`--jsonargs null -- invalid`) also exits 2, matching the regression test in `tests/shtest:210-221`
- Valid JSON args still work; `make check` results identical to baseline (5 pass / 2 pre-existing fails)
